WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.371 --> 00:00:17.012
young Lorenzo gave Leo a bag of coins.

2
00:00:18.253 --> 00:00:20.714
Mandy and Vinnie ate their cake politely.

3
00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:25.997
"Leo, take this to Master Verrocchio," Lorenzo said.

4
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.198
"And come back tomorrow.

5
00:00:29.379 --> 00:00:31.360
I hear you are a genius with machines.

6
00:00:32.724 --> 00:00:34.626
I want you to do something for me."

7
00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:40.570
As they left the Medici Palace, Mandy was excited.

8
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.832
"He's going to be a great ruler!"

9
00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:45.053
she blurted out.

10
00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:51.397
"He's only seventeen," said Leo, staring curiously at her.

11
00:00:52.558 --> 00:00:55.260
But Mandy had learned about Lorenzo in school.

12
00:00:56.821 --> 00:01:01.404
Under his rule, Florence became the most important city of the time.

13
00:01:02.576 --> 00:01:06.737
"If I were you, I would take his offer," she said to Leo.

14
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:11.138
He laughed and replied, "Are you a fortune teller?

15
00:01:12.139 --> 00:01:13.539
Can you tell the future?"

16
00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:16.940
Vinnie squeezed Mandy's arm.

17
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.461
"Hey, don't say any more," he whispered.

18
00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:25.482
"I want to show you something," Leo said.

19
00:01:26.562 --> 00:01:29.383
He took them to a huge dome-shaped building.

20
00:01:29.403 --> 00:01:31.944
"Isn't it beautiful?"

21
00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:35.550
The building was a large cathedral.

22
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:39.853
The marble panels outside were light green and pink.

23
00:01:40.954 --> 00:01:43.156
The huge dome was made of red brick.

24
00:01:44.357 --> 00:01:46.559
A tall bell tower rose beside it.

25
00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:52.744
"I come here every day to sketch," Leo said, showing them his drawings.

26
00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:55.386
"What are these machines?"

27
00:01:55.986 --> 00:01:56.687
asked Vinnie.

28
00:01:57.708 --> 00:02:02.972
He expected to see drawings of the cathedral, but the pages were filled with machines.

29
00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:06.817
One sketch showed a large wooden wheel.

30
00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:09.679
Another sketch was of a crane.

31
00:02:09.699 --> 00:02:14.542
"Machines built this cathedral," Leo replied.

32
00:02:14.562 --> 00:02:20.045
"To me machines are more fascinating than the buildings they make."

33
00:02:21.425 --> 00:02:25.067
Again Vinnie and Mandy were amazed at his talent.

34
00:02:25.087 --> 00:02:29.470
"Come inside," said Leo.

35
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.252
"There are beautiful paintings and stained glass."

36
00:02:34.864 --> 00:02:41.488
As they followed Leo inside, Mandy whispered, "There's something special about Leo."

37
00:02:41.508 --> 00:02:45.690
"He's just a kid with talent," said Vinnie.

38
00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:49.872
"I don't think so, Vinnie," Mandy said.

39
00:02:50.913 --> 00:02:52.674
She stopped and looked around.

40
00:02:52.694 --> 00:02:57.176
"Vinnie! I think we're close to the end of our journey."

41
00:02:58.297 --> 00:03:00.918
They could see beautiful stained-glass windows.

42
00:03:02.039 --> 00:03:04.000
Tall arches curved above them.

43
00:03:05.496 --> 00:03:09.459
"I think this is the place in the photo," Mandy whispered.

44
00:03:09.479 --> 00:03:12.461
"Come look," Leo called.

45
00:03:13.502 --> 00:03:18.145
He sat, opened his notebook, and began to draw with his left hand.

46
00:03:19.266 --> 00:03:24.030
Mandy watched him sketch and said, "You're so talented!"

47
00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.032
"Even for a lefty?"

48
00:03:27.592 --> 00:03:28.393
Leo grinned.

49
00:03:28.413 --> 00:03:31.115
"Who cares if you are left-handed?"

50
00:03:31.615 --> 00:03:32.316
asked Vinnie.

51
00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:37.403
"Many people think left-handed people are weird," replied Leo.

52
00:03:37.423 --> 00:03:40.004
"But it doesn't bother me."

53
00:03:41.385 --> 00:03:44.887
He got up, leaving his notebook open on the floor.

54
00:03:44.907 --> 00:03:50.430
"I want to see some paintings in the dome," he said and walked off.

55
00:03:51.891 --> 00:03:55.813
Mandy leaned over the open notebook and tried to read the writing.

56
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:59.816
"I can't tell what it says," she said.

57
00:04:00.877 --> 00:04:03.036
"The writing is so strange!"
